// These are imagined family, chosen-kin, and community histories—not claims about source canon.
// Each begins three generations before the familiar cast; kinship may be literal, chosen, or communal.
const histories={
gatsby:['A circle of workers, renters, and neighbors around the bay',['Before the bright parties, a shoreline household keeps a ledger of wages, borrowed rooms, and promises made by people with very different amounts of money.','Their children move between service, city work, and new fortunes. A neighbor’s account of who paid for each polished room becomes an inheritance of its own.','One generation later, the young learn that a name can open doors—and hide the labor behind them. They are not yet the people of the familiar story, but the bay’s old inequalities are already shaping its choices.']],
flies:['A school community and the households that send children into its care',['Long before the island, families and caretakers pass down practical knowledge: how to share food, settle a quarrel, and notice who has been left out.','A later generation grows up amid adult rules that reward obedience more readily than listening. Some keep the old lessons alive in kitchens, classrooms, and games.','By the time the children of the familiar story are born, they inherit both the possibility of cooperation and habits of hierarchy they did not choose.']],
'animal-farm':['A community of farm animals across changing owners and seasons',['Before the rebellion is imaginable, older animals teach where food is stored, which fences fail, and how work is divided. Their memory is practical—and easy for a new authority to dismiss.','Their young see rules change with each season. Some begin repeating the old warnings; others learn that a written promise means little if only a few can read it.','The generation before the familiar farm story inherits a dream of fairness alongside the hard lesson that power can rewrite memory.']],
'swiss-family':['A family tradition of making do, learning, and mutual care',['Several generations before the familiar household, relatives and neighbors preserve maps, recipes, repairs, and stories of journeys that went wrong as well as right.','A later generation turns those lessons into habits: divide the work, ask what everyone needs, and treat a new place as something to understand rather than own.','By the time the familiar family’s children arrive, they inherit curiosity and resourcefulness—but also the responsibility to decide what kind of home their skills will build.']],
'treasure-island':['A port-side network of sailors, innkeepers, and shore families',['Long before the map appears, a harbor household learns that useful knowledge travels by word of mouth: which captains pay fairly, which promises need checking, and who can be trusted in a storm.','Their children enter a port where adventure and exploitation share the same bright language. A few keep careful records; others make alliances so no one must rely on a stranger’s charm alone.','The next generation grows up hearing sea stories—and warnings that treasure is never worth more than the people asked to risk their lives for it.']],
'west-side':['Two neighborhood networks shaped by migration, work, and changing borders',['Before the young dancers are born, families and chosen kin build lives in a city that keeps changing its rents, languages, and boundaries. They trade childcare, meals, and local knowledge across streets others label as divides.','A later generation faces pressure to prove loyalty by distrusting its neighbors. Elders remember how often outsiders benefit when working people are set against one another.','The young inherit both a rich sense of belonging and a feud already older than they are. Whether that history becomes a wall or a warning is not settled yet.']],
romeo:['Two households and the wider community around an old feud',['Generations before the young lovers, a dispute over status and influence begins to harden into a family story. The first witnesses remember practical grievances, not an eternal hatred.','Children inherit the feud as a rule of belonging. Some relatives quietly keep friendships across it; others fear that questioning the story will endanger the household.','By the time the familiar young people are born, the quarrel has become an inheritance no child agreed to receive—and no child should have to resolve alone.']],
'charlottes-web':['A farm community of animals, caretakers, and small acts of attention',['Long before the familiar barn friends, generations pass along quiet knowledge of seasons, shelter, and which lives are treated as useful only when they serve someone else.','A later generation makes a practice of noticing the small and overlooked: a safe corner, a shared warning, a life worth protecting beyond its market value.','The youngest have not yet arrived, but the barn already holds an inheritance of companionship—and the question of whether care can change the rules around it.']],
huck:['A river community of families, workers, and people seeking freedom',['Before the familiar raft journey, generations along the river share routes, food, and news. Some are denied freedom by law; their knowledge and choices persist despite systems built to control them.','A later generation witnesses laws and customs presented as unquestionable. Within families and chosen networks, people teach each other to read danger, seek allies, and name injustice plainly.','The children of the familiar story are not yet born. They will inherit both the river’s routes to possibility and a society whose cruelties demand more than private kindness.']],
oliver:['A city neighborhood of working families and mutual-aid households',['Long before the familiar child is born, city families make networks of care amid scarce wages, crowded rooms, and institutions that treat poverty as a personal fault.','A later generation shares meals, work, warnings, and temporary shelter. They know that one act of rescue matters, but cannot by itself repair the conditions that make rescue necessary.','The next child inherits a city of sharp risks and generous people—and a question the adults have not answered: who will make safety something everyone can count on?']],
'king-and-i':['A household of teachers, court workers, and local scholars',['Before the familiar court and classroom meet, generations preserve knowledge through family teaching, local scholarship, and careful negotiation with distant powers.','A later generation sees outsiders mistake unfamiliar customs for ignorance. Relatives and mentors teach children to ask who is speaking, who is being translated, and who holds authority.','The young of the familiar story have not yet been born, but they will enter a world already shaped by unequal power and by people who have long been thinking for themselves.']],
'sound-music':['A household of musicians, caregivers, and neighbors in a changing Europe',['Generations before the familiar family, songs, work, and shared rituals help relatives stay connected through political change. They pass down not only melodies but practical ways to care for one another.','A later generation watches public life grow more coercive. Some learn that keeping a household safe requires quiet planning, trusted allies, and room for every member to speak.','The children of the familiar story are still in the future. Their inheritance is music and affection, but also the knowledge that joy needs courage and a plan when power turns threatening.']],
alice:['A family of storytellers, puzzle-makers, and curious children',['Long before the familiar child follows a hurried rabbit, relatives and chosen kin trade puzzles and stories that let children question rules without being punished for wondering.','A later generation grows up among adults who sometimes confuse good manners with unquestioning obedience. A few keep wonder alive as a way to notice when a rule makes no sense.','The next child is not yet born. They will inherit a world of strange instructions—and the permission, if someone passes it on, to ask who made them.']],
'mary-poppins':['A city household and its circle of caregivers across generations',['Before the familiar family, generations of city caregivers learn how to make time for children in streets and homes organized around adult work. Songs and games carry attention across busy days.','A later generation inherits schedules that leave little room for listening. Neighbors and relatives quietly preserve rituals of play, noticing that children’s worries do not disappear just because adults are occupied.','The familiar children are not yet born, but they will inherit both the pressure of a hurried household and a tradition of making wonder—and attention—part of ordinary life.']],
'charlie-wonka':['A working family and the neighborhood that shares its table',['Long before the golden ticket, a family and its neighbors stretch small resources through shared meals, practical skills, and stories that make scarcity less lonely.','A later generation sees wealth celebrated as spectacle while the people doing essential work remain out of sight. They pass on the belief that delight means more when it is shared fairly.','The child of the familiar story is still years away. Their inheritance includes hope, humor, and a clear-eyed question about who gets to enjoy a wonder built by many hands.']],
wonka:['A line of makers, market sellers, and chosen collaborators',['Generations before the young inventor arrives, makers trade recipes and craft knowledge while learning how guilds and gatekeepers can restrict who gets to sell their work.','A later generation experiments together, sharing credit and warning one another about bargains that turn friendship into unpaid labor. Their small collaborations keep a different kind of business imaginable.','The young dreamer has not yet been born. They will inherit both ambition and a community lesson: invention is not a triumph if its costs are pushed onto unseen helpers.']],
'gone-with-wind':['Black families and a wider community navigating enslavement, emancipation, and its aftermath',['Generations before the familiar characters, enslaved Black families build kinship, knowledge, and care under a violent system that denies their freedom and often tears families apart. Their lives and choices are not a backdrop to someone else’s story.','After emancipation, a later generation pursues family reunification, safety, education, fair wages, and land amid organized efforts to restrict those freedoms. Community networks carry skills and memory where institutions fail them.','The familiar cast is not yet born. The world they will enter is already shaped by slavery’s violence and by Black people’s agency, resistance, and ongoing struggle for material freedom.']],
casablanca:['A North African neighborhood network of families, port workers, and newcomers',['Before the familiar café, generations in a port community build ties across languages and arrivals. They keep routes, contacts, and food moving when official borders make ordinary life precarious.','A later generation faces shifting authorities and new waves of people seeking safety. Neighbors debate how to help without turning refuge into a favor owed.','The familiar travelers are still in the future. They will inherit a city whose hospitality and compromises were shaped by generations of people making room under pressure.']],
northwest:['A family of clerks, station workers, and people whose names are often overlooked',['Long before the mistaken identity, generations of ordinary workers learn how a missing record or an assumed name can alter a person’s safety. They preserve details others consider too small to matter.','A later generation works among institutions that prize confident explanations. Their household teaches caution: verify a claim, keep your own account, and do not confuse authority with truth.','The familiar strangers are not yet born. They will enter a world where people can be mistaken for pieces in someone else’s plan—and where careful witnesses can change what happens.']],
'maltese-falcon':['A neighborhood circle of office workers, porters, and independent tradespeople',['Before the famous object changes hands, generations of workers around the city learn to read contracts, clients, and the difference between a polished story and a reliable one.','A later generation keeps shared records and practical alliances, especially for those whose expertise is ignored until it becomes useful to someone powerful.','The familiar investigators are not yet born. They will inherit a city where trust is negotiated, evidence can be buried, and overlooked people may see the decisive detail first.']],
'death-on-nile':['A river community of boat workers, guides, families, and travelers',['Generations before the luxury steamer, river families sustain livelihoods through navigation, seasonal knowledge, and skilled work that wealthy visitors often mistake for scenery.','A later generation watches fortunes travel through the region while local labor remains undervalued. They teach their children to keep accounts, tell their own stories, and notice who benefits from a grand journey.','The familiar passengers are not yet born. Their mystery will unfold on a river already carrying many lives and histories beyond the guests’ view.']],
'orient-express':['A railway community of workers, travelers, and families along the route',['Before the snowbound train, generations of railway workers and their families build lives around timetables, repair skills, and routes linking distant communities. Their labor makes other people’s journeys possible.','A later generation sees borders and official rules determine whose movement is easy and whose is questioned. Workers quietly share information and help one another stay safe across stations.','The familiar passengers have not yet been born. They will inherit a network held together by unseen labor—and a question about whose account counts when authority arrives.']]
};
