 {id:'rambo',title:'First Blood: The Road Back',author:'An original reimagining inspired by the film character',genre:'Survival & belonging',icon:'🌲',category:'ideas',cast:[['John Rambo','A veteran searching for a place to rest','Highly capable and guarded, carrying grief and alarm that do not vanish just because the danger has passed.'],['Sarah','A local volunteer offering practical help','Patient but not sentimental, willing to listen while respecting that trust cannot be demanded.'],['Deputy Mitch','A deputy caught between orders and conscience','Wary of uncertainty, with a choice between escalating fear and making room for another account.']],history:['A rural community of veterans, repair workers, and families who carry difficult memories',['Three generations before the familiar veteran returns, families in a mountain town share land, tools, and seasonal work. Their elders remember earlier conflicts and teach practical skills, while leaving many painful experiences unnamed.','Their children face economic change and new wars. A volunteer aid circle begins helping injured workers and returning service members, but the town’s pride still often mistakes silence for healing.','One generation before the story, the community has inherited both resourcefulness and a gap in its care: it knows how to survive emergencies better than how to welcome people home afterward.']],scenes:[['A roadside greeting','A veteran walks through a town that seems to have forgotten how to greet strangers. A deputy’s questions tighten into suspicion; a volunteer offers food and a quiet place.','When a person is treated as a threat before being heard, how can safety be restored without denying anyone’s fear?',[['Accept the quiet offer and explain only what feels safe','Let trust begin in small steps','caution','You made room for connection without pretending the past was simple.'],['Ask the deputy to state the concern and the next step plainly','Replace vague suspicion with accountability','discernment','You asked authority to be specific before you accepted its power.']]],['The forest line','A misunderstanding becomes a pursuit. The woods offer cover, but every move risks turning fear into injury. People search from different sides, each believing they are protecting someone.','Skill can keep you alive; what keeps survival from becoming another kind of isolation?',[['Leave a clear signal and a safe route for others','Make your way back visible','care','You used hard-won skill to reduce danger for everyone.'],['Keep distance and wait for a calm contact','Refuse a panicked confrontation','restraint','You chose not to let urgency dictate another irreversible moment.']]],['The room with the lights on','The immediate danger has passed, but the memories have not. A trusted person can stay, listen, and help find support; no single conversation can repair everything.','What does returning mean when home has not yet learned how to receive you?',[['Name what you can and ask for ongoing help','Let healing be shared work','honesty','You let the truth be a beginning, not a demand for instant recovery.'],['Set a boundary and choose one safe next step','Keep agency in the aftermath','self-preservation','You chose a manageable future over someone else’s timetable.']]]]},
 {id:'terminator',title:'The Terminator: A Human Choice',author:'An original reimagining inspired by the film character',genre:'Identity & responsibility',icon:'⚙️',category:'adventure',cast:[['The protector','A machine learning the difference between command and care','Precise and newly curious, confronted with the fact that keeping someone safe also means respecting their choices.'],['Sarah Connor','A young woman whose future has been decided by others','Resourceful and frightened, determined to become more than a warning in someone else’s story.'],['Kyle Reese','A messenger from a brutal possible future','Devoted and exhausted, carrying a certainty that may protect or overwhelm the person he means to help.']],history:['A line of mechanics, signal keepers, and ordinary people deciding what tools are for',['Three generations before the threatened future, mechanics and radio operators teach their children to repair shared tools and question who controls them. A machine is valued for the lives it supports, not for the force it can exert.','Their descendants enter an age of automation and centralized power. Some build safeguards and keep written records; others accept convenience without asking who bears the risk when systems fail.','One generation before the familiar crisis, a handful of workers pass on a stubborn principle: no instruction is more important than the human consequences of obeying it.']],scenes:[['A warning without proof','A stranger insists that Sarah is in danger and offers only fragments of an impossible explanation. A relentless pursuer follows; certainty and panic threaten to make every choice for her.','Can protection be real if the person being protected has no say?',[['Give Sarah the evidence you can verify and let her decide','Turn warning into informed choice','transparency','You made knowledge a tool she could hold, not a leash.'],['Move her toward a public, staffed place before explaining','Reduce immediate danger without demanding trust','safety','You chose a safer setting, though unanswered questions still weigh between you.']]],['The command inside','A machine built to obey begins to notice the difference between an order and a person. A route is blocked; force might clear it, but bystanders are close.','If you can act, what gives you the right to decide how?',[['Find a route that keeps bystanders out of harm','Let restraint shape capability','restraint','You proved that ability without judgment is not protection.'],['Ask Sarah to choose between the real risks','Share authority under pressure','partnership','You made the plan stronger by treating her as its co-author.']]],['A future not yet written','The danger recedes, but tomorrow remains uncertain. Sarah wants a life that is hers; the protector must decide whether its purpose ends with the immediate threat.','Can a legacy be protected without being controlled?',[['Offer the truth and stand back while Sarah chooses','Respect a future you cannot own','respect','You let protection end where another person’s agency begins.'],['Stay available by invitation, not command','Make care accountable','care','You offered continuity without turning it into surveillance.']]]]},
 {id:'predator',title:'Predator: The Shape of Courage',author:'An original reimagining inspired by the film characters',genre:'Survival & teamwork',icon:'🌿',category:'adventure',cast:[['Dutch Schaefer','A team leader facing an unknown hunter','Decisive and physically brave, learning that leadership is measured by who gets heard and brought home.'],['Anna','A local survivor who understands the terrain','Watchful and self-possessed, unwilling to be reduced to a clue or a prize.'],['Mac','A skilled teammate carrying old grief','Loyal and volatile, alert to danger but at risk of letting loss dictate the next move.']],history:['A forest-edge community of guides, medics, and people who know the land',['Three generations before the expedition, families living near the forest pass down knowledge of weather, plants, and safe travel. Their guides teach visitors that the land is inhabited and understood, not an empty arena.','Their children see outsiders arrive with maps that leave local names out. A network of guides and healers records routes and shares warnings, while trying to protect the community’s right to decide who enters.','One generation before the familiar team arrives, the inheritance is clear: survival depends on listening to local knowledge, and courage without humility can make danger for everyone.']],scenes:[['A mission changes shape','A rescue assignment becomes a hunt. The team finds evidence that its original briefing left out the people and risks already present in the forest.','What does a leader owe the people who were never included in the plan?',[['Pause and ask Anna what the evidence means','Let local knowledge revise the mission','humility','You let expertise come from experience, not rank.'],['Account for every teammate and set a return point','Put people before the objective','responsibility','You made the team’s safety part of the mission rather than an afterthought.']]],['The unseen movement','Something moves beyond sight. The team’s strength can become a trap if everyone acts alone; grief and suspicion begin to split attention.','When fear narrows the world, what helps a group stay human?',[['Share observations and coordinate a retreat','Make information common property','solidarity','You turned separate instincts into a plan people could trust.'],['Draw the danger away from the least protected','Take a deliberate risk for others','bravery','You chose courage with a purpose, not for an audience.']]],['The last clearing','The survivors reach a clearing where escape is possible, but someone must remain long enough to make it safe. The unknown threat has not made every person an enemy.','How do you leave without carrying the violence forward?',[['Choose escape together and account for everyone','Refuse to abandon the group','community','You made survival a shared promise rather than a private prize.'],['Offer a final warning and refuse needless pursuit','End the cycle where you can','mercy','You chose not to confuse victory with making more victims.']]]]},
 {id:'conan',title:'Conan: The Forge and the Road',author:'An original reimagining inspired by the film character',genre:'Power & freedom',icon:'🔥',category:'ideas',cast:[['Conan','A wanderer shaped by loss and labor','Strong, suspicious of rulers, and deciding whether freedom means living without bonds or choosing what to protect.'],['Valeria','A thief and companion who insists on equal terms','Bold and practical, unwilling to be treated as an ornament in another person’s legend.'],['Subotai','An archer who knows the value of chosen kin','Dry-witted and loyal, wary of promises that ask one person to sacrifice for another’s glory.']],history:['A mountain community of smiths, storytellers, and people displaced by rulers',['Three generations before the wanderer is born, a mountain community makes tools and keeps oral histories of raids, migrations, and the names of people who never returned. Its elders teach that strength can build shelter as surely as it can break a gate.','Their descendants are scattered by a ruler’s demand for labor and tribute. Chosen kin preserve songs and techniques, passing on warnings about leaders who call obedience peace.','One generation before the familiar road begins, the community leaves an inheritance of skill and defiance, but also a grief that can turn survival into a life organized only around revenge.']],scenes:[['The chain at the gate','A fortified town offers safety to those who accept its ruler’s protection. The gate is open for you, but the people behind it pay for every promise in labor and silence.','Is freedom only escape, or does it include what you do for those still inside?',[['Help the workers plan a safe way to refuse the levy','Make resistance collective','solidarity','You made rebellion answer to the people who would bear its cost.'],['Leave before the ruler can bind you','Keep your freedom from being bargained away','freedom','You refused a gilded cage, though those left behind remain in your thoughts.']]],['The campfire bargain','A companion proposes a risky theft from the ruler’s storehouse. The plan could buy passage for many, but its danger is being carried unevenly.','What makes a band of outcasts a fellowship rather than another hierarchy?',[['Set the risk and reward openly with everyone','Share the terms','equity','You made loyalty measurable in fair treatment.'],['Reject the raid and find a slower route','Refuse to spend others without consent','prudence','You accepted delay rather than hide the cost of a bold plan.']]],['The broken idol','The ruler’s power is weakened. Those who suffered want different futures; vengeance is tempting, but a new throne could repeat the old bargain.','What do you build after breaking the thing that held you?',[['Return decision-making to the people who live there','Leave power in local hands','justice','You made freedom more than a change of ruler.'],['Take the road with your companions and refuse the crown','Choose chosen kin over dominion','humility','You declined to become what your anger had opposed.']]]]},
